-- More COSMOS briefings from the client localization
-- +migrate Up

UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Alright, in that case maybe I do have a minute or two. But hold on a second while I do a trace for bugs on you. Stand still... 
Okay, you''re clean. What is it? And keep your voice down.' WHERE missionID=93000 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Bring Bartezo''s message to Lord Manel. Bartezo is located in Port Maphante in Garisas.' WHERE missionID=93036 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Ader Finn tells me in his message that the operation against Manel was not authorized by the highest ranking order of the Blood Raiders, even though members of the organization were involved. This was simply a side-job taken by one of the Blood Raider commanders in Araz, Kardour Maxten. Not only that but Ader reports that rumor in the organization has it that Kardour and the other commanders have had heated exchanges about his involvement in the Manel incident.
This is good news for us, because it means Ader can possibly acquire the help of one of the other Blood Raider commanders in our investigation, indirectly of course. He claims to be rather close to one of these commanders, who has access to a key which should temporarily disable the trap at the acceleration gate leading into Manel''s Mansion. But there is a price of course, Ader was asked to assassinate Kardour in exchange for this key. The Blood Raider commander who he has been in touch with is apparently a rival of Kardour''s, and is terrified that Blood Raider involvement in the killing or kidnapping of Manel will compromise their entire operation in Araz.
Obviously you are the best canditate to take out Kardour. I will supply you with a bookmark which was included in Ader''s message, it should lead you to him. But I warn you, he operates a battleship and might be too tough for you to handle alone. Good luck.' WHERE missionID=93042 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='We Amarrians are nothing if not civilized. We were eating off of gilded plates while the other races were still using their hands to wipe their arses. We have traditions older than sin and customs more ingrained (and sometimes more disgusting) than overgrown toenails. 
The feud between House Arachnan and House Methros is getting serious, and in accordance with traditions, there''s protocol to be followed. But there''s a bit of a twist, you see. Lord Arachnan succeeded his father not many years ago. But while he is the eldest son of his line, he does have an older sibling, a sister. I believe you''ve already heard her name from me: Lady Eroza Arachnan. She is disputing her brother''s claim as the head of the Arachnan family. 
Lord Methros, in his infinite wisdom, has decided to throw his lot in with Lady Arachnan. Lord Methros'' best and brightest archivists and scholars have been poring over old documents looking for precedents, and it seems they''ve found one. Some thousand years ago, apparently, when the head of the Arachnan family passed away, he was succeeded not by his eldest son, who by all accounts was frail of mind and body, but by his eldest daughter. She was a most capable administrator and disciplinarian, I understand, as is her descendant, the admirable Lady Eroza Arachnan. Lord Methros passed these records into my hands, and I will make sure they''re well broadcast over the ACN netword in the next few days. But protocol calls for this information also to be delivered, by hand, to the lord of the region. 
That''s where you come in, <Character>. I want you to deliver the ancestral records to Kador Prime, where an associate of mine will accept them from you and deliver the package to the Kador household. The package is waiting for you in the ACN station over in Aphi, so you have to pick it up there first. This is hot news: Hurry so I can send out my report of the goings on through the ACN network.' WHERE missionID=93068 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Well ... ok, that will have to do. Now as for the information, I have something on Black Jack, yes. This guy, Tikui Makan, a prominent member of the Guristas I might add, has been boasting lately of killing Black Jack in a duel which supposedly took place in Y5J-EU. I don''t have any more information on the matter, but I can give you Tikui''s location. I''ll upload it into this data chip, take it back to Isana. And when you do that, put in a good word for me, will ya?' WHERE missionID=93386 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Welcome, young pilot. Good to see a friend of the Empire in this foul place: If my work didn''t require my being here, I would long ago have left it far behind. I do not know if your presence here shows that you possess a strong backbone or that you''re merely a fool wandering around in the lion''s maw. Perhaps we shall see. 
It may that you can be of service to me. My task here is to monitor Minmatar activity in the constellation. The Republic trundles around like a blind dinosaur, so it''s easy to track its doings. The rebels like nothing better than to boast of their heroics. But there is one group that is hard to keep tabs on, the Krusual tribe. As ever, their evasiveness makes them hard to gauge. 
My superiors have finally responded to my repeated requests for assistance and have sent one of their infiltrators out here. These guys are former Minmatar slaves, correctly trained and conditioned to act as agents on our behalf within Minmatar society. The infiltrator they sent out here is sitting in one of the Joint Harvesting stations over in Hjoramold. What I want you to do is go and pick him up there, then drop him off in one of the Krusual tribe stations in Nakugard. 
If you show yourself capable enough to perform this task without a glitch, I may have more tasks in line for you.' WHERE missionID=93402 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='You did alright on that infiltrator job. I suppose. But I''m willing to give you another chance to impress me. The Minmatars are not the only nuisance here: The pirate infestation in the constellation is astounding. I guess it just goes to show how lousy the Republic is at keeping its territories in check. 
The pirates are a constant pain the ass; sometimes it seem they have a sixth sense about where and when to be to foil my plans. If the Republic is too weak to deal with them, I guess I have to. The pirates that are proving to be the biggest pest are the ones that drop the Spy ID Slice. Kill a few of them and bring me five such insignia. You can usually find the buggers roaming in the contested complexes here in Ani. 
I''ve even gone out on several killing sprees myself in the past. Those excursions yielded me some pretty nice Minmatar ammo that I have no use for myself. You can have it as a reward when you return with those slices.' WHERE missionID=93403 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Your performance collecting those slices was adequate. Well, anyway, adequate enough for me to trust you with an important mission. The Ani constellation is crawling with all kinds of hackers and tech-freaks. While this fact makes it that much harder to ensure that communication links remain safe, it also present us with an opportunity. These hackers like to break into databanks and steal sensitive information. Usually, their pathetic ethics keep them from exploiting the information they steal. They don''t delete it, though, but store it for themselves so they can brag about their deeds to fellow hackers. 
As I see it, these hackers are sitting on a gold mine, and I think few of them even realize this. If I could get my hands on some of the stuff they''ve collected, it could lead to my promotion and even a transfer out of this hellhole. I''ve discovered a small hacker community in an old ore refinery in the Tvink system. They''ve converted the place to become something they call Hacker Haven. I shudder even to think about what that might mean. 
I want you to go over there and shoot everything to pieces. My sources inform me that inside this haven sits a little blue box that is a virtual treasure trove full of stolen data from all around the constellation. I want that box. I don''t know exactly where it might lie, unfortunately, so you''ll just have to keep shooting until you locate it. The blue box itself is supposedly indestructible, so don''t worry about that: You should be able to pluck it from the wreckage of whatever structure it was in. This mission means a lot to me, so you''ll get a fine blueprint copy as a reward if you succeed. 
Oh, did I mention that the hackers are pretty well protected? Maybe you should bring some friends along.' WHERE missionID=93404 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='There''s just one last thing that I need. I was contacted a few months ago by one of the elders within the Brutor Tribe about a rogue Sebiestor agent operating from the Carnival in Barkrik. Although I may be Sebiestor myself, I bear no love for those I used to call family. The suspected rogue agent is none other than Dagras Kutill, a filthy wench who deals in drugs and other illegal wares. 
I''ve spoken to her on numerous occasions, and in one of our conversations I stumbled upon some pretty interesting info. She claims to have discovered a way to hack into the Brutor Tribe''s station database, giving her enormous power over any Brutor station. Apparently she uses some kind of program that is stored on database chips she keeps hidden in one of her compounds. 
When I tried to ask her more questions about this program, she became extremely agitated and started accusing me of being a traitor to the Sebiestors. A few weeks later, I was almost killed by a gang of Maru thugs, and I''m sure she was behind it. She''s been after my neck ever since, so I''ve had to call in a group of Brutor mercenaries to keep me safe. Without them, I''d probably be dead by now. 
Since she doesn''t know you yet, <Character>, I''m sure you will have an easier time acquiring this data chip than me. If you do, I''ll pay a hefty price for it.' WHERE missionID=93414 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='I''m ready to take my research to the next level. But to do so I must get my hands on some decent science instruments. Without a big corp behind me, the manufacturers of these items won''t even speak to me. I''ve been scouring the second hand market, but not found anything of value. My work will soon stall if I don''t get this stuff.
I received an interesting tidbit from a former colleague of mine, one of the few still talking to me. It seems one of the secret research labs the Sisters are running in Lanngisi just had a serious accident and was abandoned. I don''t know the extent of the accident, but do know that some lethal substances leaked out. I''m sure the place is already crawling with scavengers, but if we move quickly we might get something good.
It''s funny, only a few weeks ago I would be shattered by these news, but now I hardly feel anything. All I care about is how I can exploit this disaster to my own advantage. I guess I just have learnt that to succeed in this harsh world, one must be extra tough. My sheltered life has never exposed me to this world until now, but I feel I''m coping well.
Enough about that. If you''re willing to go over to the contaminated research lab and see if you can find any science instruments, I''m sure I can find something suitable to reward you with upon your return. It doesn''t matter if the items are broken, just get me a few and I''m sure I can make something out of them. If the facility itself doesn''t yield anything you might have to take out some of the scavengers there and see if they cough something interesting up. Just make sure to blow up everything you see there to make sure you get all the salvagable items.' WHERE missionID=93480 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');

-- +migrate Down
-- (briefings stay)
